- The server maintains an in-memory object `notes` to store notes.
- When a client connects, the server sends the current notes.
- When a client updates or deletes a note, it sends a message to the server.
- The server updates its store and broadcasts the change to all other connected clients.
- Clients update their local notes and UI accordingly.
- This approach ensures minimal latency and real-time synchronization.

